2. SMILE Serve (Dual License: AGPLv3 / Commercial Enterprise)
==============================================================================

SMILE Serve (`serve`) is the high-throughput, low-latency JVM inference platform
and model serving runtime, dual-licensed under:

  a) GNU Affero General Public License version 3 (AGPLv3):
     Free for open-source systems and applications where the surrounding network
     service and infrastructure are disclosed under AGPLv3.

  b) Commercial Enterprise Runtime License:
     Enterprises deploying SMILE Serve in production microservices, high-volume
     streaming architectures (Kafka/Flink), or cloud clusters without AGPLv3
     disclosure requirements must obtain an Enterprise Runtime License.
     Enterprise licenses include high-availability clustering, zero-GC optimizations,
     dedicated SLAs, CVE hotfix guarantees, and legal indemnification.

==============================================================================
3. SMILE Studio (Business Source License 1.1 / Commercial)
==============================================================================

SMILE Studio (`studio`) is an agentic data science desktop IDE and model-packaging
environment licensed under the Business Source License 1.1 (BSL 1.1).

  - Use Grant: You may use SMILE Studio free of charge for non-commercial
    evaluation, personal learning, academic research, data exploration, and
    exporting serialized model packages.
  - Commercial & Production Use: Use of SMILE Studio within commercial
    organizations beyond evaluation, or redistribution as part of a commercial
    product, requires a paid commercial license from HALO.AI, LLC.
  - Change License: After four (4) years from the release date of each respective
    version, that version automatically converts to the GNU Affero General Public
    License version 3.0 (AGPLv3) or later.

